# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# www -> apex is NOT handled here, and cannot be. Cloudflare Pages matches
# _redirects on the PATH only, so a source with a hostname in it is silently
# ignored — a rule written here does nothing at all, which is the worst kind
# of not working.
#
# It is instead a Redirect Rule on the zone, created 2026-09-07 and verified
# live the same day:
#
#   Cloudflare > builtbytyler.com > Rules > Redirect Rules
#     Name    Redirect www to apex (301)
#     Match   wildcard  https://www.builtbytyler.com/*
#     Then    301 to    https://builtbytyler.com/${1}
#     Preserve query string: on
#
#   https://www.builtbytyler.com/shop            -> 301 https://builtbytyler.com/shop
#   https://www.builtbytyler.com/software?utm=x  -> 301 ...software?utm=x   (query kept)
#   http://www.builtbytyler.com/about            -> 200 apex in two hops
#
# The two hops on plain http are expected and fine: "Always Use HTTPS" runs
# first and upgrades http://www -> https://www, and this rule then takes it
# to the apex. Matching http here as well would need a custom filter
# expression, and the ordering between that and Always Use HTTPS is not
# guaranteed — a chain of two is not worth trading for a rule that might
# not fire.
#
# This file is kept because PATH redirects (an old URL moving, say) do work
# here and belong in it.

# The reverse engineering page became Games on 2026-10-18.
/reverse-engineering /games 301
/reverse-engineering.html /games 301

